# Agent panel UI patterns

## Chat panel (`AgentChatPanel.tsx`)

### Markdown rendering
Assistant messages use `<ChatMarkdown>` — a JSX-based renderer (no external library). It handles:
- Fenced code blocks ` ``` ` → `<pre><code>`
- `**bold**`, `*italic*`, `` `inline code` ``
- Bullet / ordered lists, headings (`#`, `##`, `###`), `---` rules
- Auto-linked `https://` URLs and `[text](url)` links

User messages stay as plain text (`white-space: pre-wrap`).

### Copy button
`<button className="agent-chat__copy">` sits inside `.agent-chat__bubble-wrap` — opacity 0, revealed on parent hover (CSS). Uses `navigator.clipboard.writeText()`. Shows `<Check>` for 1.8s after copy.

### Starter prompts
Shown when `messages.length === 0 && !runMutation.isPending`:
- `STARTER_PROMPTS` array of `{ label, text }` defined at file top
- Grid: `.agent-chat__starters-grid` (2-col)
- Clicking sets `input` state — does not auto-send

Add new starters directly to `STARTER_PROMPTS` — no API needed.

### CSS classes
`.agent-chat__md`, `.agent-chat__copy`, `.agent-chat__starters`, `.agent-chat__starter` — all in `index.css` under the `/* markdown inside assistant bubbles */` block.

